# UpscaleCloud.comp: the clouds are drawn at a fraction of the screen's pixels and filled in over the frames, each
# pixel blending what was drawn this frame into its history, read from where it was on the last frame. The history
# counts only when that place is on screen, which IsUVOnScreen takes to be between the centres of the outermost pixels.
# The camera moving even slightly towards an edge puts an outermost pixel's last place in its own outer half: off
# screen by that test, the pixel starts its history again and shows one noisy sample each frame, a line of a pixel
# flickering along that edge over clouds (twice the frame-to-frame change of the clouds beside it). The history covers
# the whole screen and is read with clamping, so the fix takes the screen's edges as its bounds.

@@ edit cloud-edges Clouds/Upscaling/UpscalingFunctions.glsl
@@ what took the screen's edges as the bounds of the clouds' history
@@ find
    vec2 minUV = HALF_TEXEL_OFFSET * invScreenResolution;
    vec2 maxUV = vec2(1.0) - minUV;
@@ replace
    // macOS port: the screen's edges, not the outermost pixels' centres, or those pixels lose their history
    vec2 minUV = vec2(0.0);
    vec2 maxUV = vec2(1.0);
